{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch","id":1517736,"title":"Should you be able to kill the Patriarch?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-11T20:50:31-07:00","id":1517736,"title":"Should you be able to kill the Patriarch?","content":"Should the Patriarch be something you can off like a Maeljin Incarna, and if so then what would his weakness be? Also, where would you go looking for him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T23:50:32-07:00","id":1517740,"title":"","content":"Tough one<br /> Depending the interpretation ,really<br /> The Patriarch is, according the Black Furies, the Incarna of jealous men, and a servant of Abhorra, the Urge Wyrm of hatred - if you take this, then he probably is in Malfeas<br /> Well ,we &quot;know&quot; it is not &quot;true&quot;<br /> The Patriarch is in fact a facet of the Weaver, representing Dogma - encourages the blind ritualization of life, harsh guidelines, and equally harsh punishments against transgressors of any kind. From him, mankind learned to evaluate certain ideals over others.<br /> The Patriarch (or Dogma) is a very old, and very strong concept, even the Garou are his followers in a sense becasue their whole life and society built around a set of dogmas, the Litany<br /> Killing him would be difficult and probably would usher Chaos. But his weakness would be this rigidity and the laws and dogmas inherent built-in contradictions<br /> A bit like the old divide 0 problem for the computers<br /> The Patriarch/Dogma is so rigid, it can't change, can't bend, can't adapt, or just very slowly. Facing with the contradictions and systematically destroying his source of power, eg. relegion would strenghten other Weaver avatars, while weaken The Patriarch/Dogma - I think this is supported by the fact the influence of the Patriarch was strongest during the Dark Ages and the early Renaissance, but has diminished in later years, only to rise again thanks to growing fundamentalist movements in various religions.<br /> The Weaver has three Incarna: The Machine (the manifestation of her gift of Technology), the Patriarch (the manifestation of Dogma), and Science (the manifestation of Science, of course).<br /> By demolish Relegion would strengthen Science and even the Machine, technology and science don't have room for relegion and relegious dogmas<br /> Relegion is the most &quot;dogmatic&quot;, but per definition Dogma is a principle or set of principles laid down by an authority as incontrovertibly true.<br /> So the Patriarch as the manifestation of Dogma is a slipery eel when it comes to weakining him but not impossible - even could be killable I think<br /> <br /> Where you can find him?<br /> I would say in the CyberRealm, in the center of Spider City, on the top with his &quot;brothers&quot; Science and Technology, in a gigantic techno-church like structure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T03:07:44-07:00","id":1517750,"title":"","content":"I think that those two may actually be different entities. There are many things in the Umbra that represent different facets of the same concepts. The Wicked Patriarch of Malfeas may coexist with the Patriarch of the Weaver and a totemic ancestral human protector known as the Patriarch.<br /> <br /> Killing spirits of great concepts is never easy, and even if you manage to do it permanently, the concepts will still exist and new spirits will fill the void. After all, Werewolves kill banes of pain, suffering, disease and abuse on a daily basis, yet it doesn't make the World of Darkness any brighter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T03:38:34-07:00","id":1517753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517750#post1517750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Killing spirits of great concepts is never easy, and even if you manage to do it permanently, the concepts will still exist and new spirits will fill the void. After all, Werewolves kill banes of pain, suffering, disease and abuse on a daily basis, yet it doesn't make the World of Darkness any brighter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I treat major Incarna and up as something that can not really be destroyed unless the concept behind them ceases to exist or is severely weakened. A bit like the chaos gods in Warhammer 40k; you have better chances (although still minuscle) of changing the general understanding of a concept than outright destroying it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T05:40:39-07:00","id":1517755,"title":"","content":"Killing it is a tricky concept with something so big. Like the roman empire rather than a person. What you might be able is temporarily destroy its spirit on the knowledge it will reform at a later date like the Maijin ultimately would. This is certainly a net positive if you pull it off.<br /> permanently killing or making it less awful would require that to be followed up with changes in human society, which would actually be easier if he's currently 'dead/dormant' he could be whittled down this way over centuries.<br /> <br /> think of it like the decline of the roman empire which in practice took over a 1000 years from the third century crisis to the fall of constanople.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T07:58:43-07:00","id":1517770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517750#post1517750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that those two may actually be different entities. There are many things in the Umbra that represent different facets of the same concepts. The Wicked Patriarch of Malfeas may coexist with the Patriarch of the Weaver and a totemic ancestral human protector known as the Patriarch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans have totens?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T08:01:22-07:00","id":1517771,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> I think that's an excellent comparison. I'd say that killing such a concept would definitely create room to make changes and would alleviate some effects for a while. But doing it right and understanding how to make full use of an opportunity would be an epic quest in and of itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T08:08:58-07:00","id":1517774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517771#post1517771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> I think that's an excellent comparison. I'd say that killing such a concept would definitely create room to make changes and would alleviate some effects for a while. But doing it right and understanding how to make full use of an opportunity would be an epic quest in and of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or give opportunity to something even worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T09:01:33-07:00","id":1517787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517774#post1517774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or give opportunity to something even worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>By default everything in WoD always gets worse. So you may as well focus on trying to make things better. If anything the Garou have proven they can be better, and it's the goal of the final generation to be the ones to make it count.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517770#post1517770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Humans have totens?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits subsist on offerings, reverence and worship. Anything that was ever worshipped and treated with great love and respect exists in the Umbra. Be it the car someone took 10 years to rebuild by hand after their father's accident or a God. Whether it came to be in the Umbra from these emotions or something else identified itself as such and took on the characteristics it needed to have is open to discussion. Anything and everything that entities in the &quot;real&quot; world ever cared for exists in the umbra. Totems aren't just a mechanic in the game, they are an anthropological and cultural link to who humans were and what and how they worshipped.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T10:02:46-07:00","id":1517792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517774#post1517774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or give opportunity to something even worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly but despite wods relentlessly (sometimes tediously) pessimistic outlook wod has a rough logic to it.<br /> the 'destruction' of an incarna results in am irl knock on effect were the concepts it represents become irl weaker. It's why garou are very keen to kill maejin. Killing the patriarch would weaken dogma which in turn would make it easier to weaken it irl. Husbands become slightly less controlling, Southern Baptists focus more on 'love' etc and then you push forward on that. Probably has additional knock on affects to stuff like wyrm stuff like hate and self loathing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-12-2023, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T11:00:41-07:00","id":1517796,"title":"","content":"Given that for 2.5 editions ParaWolfOnyx didn't write a SINGLE 'a Garou killed Methaluseah&quot; duel*... You know the answer.<br /> *ShyHorus vs Seth doesn't count - it's to vague-written and unclear to serve as example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T12:12:36-07:00","id":1517803,"title":"","content":"The follow-up is important though - the Patriarch dying would certainly create a wave of freedom, sexism would be less vitriolic, men less controlling, women less likely to serve as handmaidens of patriarchy (in many situations women serve as the main enforcers of patriarchy), but humanity would need to learn from it and change and make good use of the spiritual reprieve.<br /> <br /> If it's a nice holiday, but ultimately humanity doesn't capitalize on the opportunity, things will gradually return to how they were. A similar spirit will rise up to fill the gap, perhaps with a slightly different set of quirks. A long lasting and genuine grass roots change would need to follow, and that's endless, little, global work that is the work of whole networks of Septs and charities and faiths and so on.<br /> <br /> Basically if a group of heroic Garou kill a powerful conceptual spirit, an evil one such as Patriarch or one of the Lords of the Wyrmish Elements, the real battle is fought by humanity itself in the aftermath; are they worthy of the new hand they've been dealt, or will they go back to more of the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T12:45:40-07:00","id":1517807,"title":"","content":"Well....what if I make a start on a bunch of local MRA groups and we'll check back in a month as to how its going. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T14:01:18-07:00","id":1517818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517807#post1517807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well....what if I make a start on a bunch of local MRA groups and we'll check back in a month as to how its going. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mra is more the mixture of the nameless angel, hellbringer and doge klypse. Father domain requires a degree of success lacking in MRA's. Personally I'd recommend working on the terfs and pushing for police reform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-12-2023, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T16:39:38-07:00","id":1517842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517787#post1517787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By default everything in WoD always gets worse. So you may as well focus on trying to make things better. If anything the Garou have proven they can be better, and it's the goal of the final generation to be the ones to make it count.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Spirits subsist on offerings, reverence and worship. Anything that was ever worshipped and treated with great love and respect exists in the Umbra. Be it the car someone took 10 years to rebuild by hand after their father's accident or a God. Whether it came to be in the Umbra from these emotions or something else identified itself as such and took on the characteristics it needed to have is open to discussion. Anything and everything that entities in the &quot;real&quot; world ever cared for exists in the umbra. Totems aren't just a mechanic in the game, they are an anthropological and cultural link to who humans were and what and how they worshipped.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just that I recently re-read part of the silver fang book and there is a mention that humans wouldn't have a totem for them or a patronus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T16:45:35-07:00","id":1517844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517787#post1517787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By default everything in WoD always gets worse. So you may as well focus on trying to make things better. If anything the Garou have proven they can be better, and it's the goal of the final generation to be the ones to make it count.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but to be quite honest, I think a Garou's definition of making things &quot;better&quot; can be quite problematic, that said it got to the point of them replacing partriarch, I can think of a few lines of thinking of theirs that would get you into trouble.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T17:11:58-07:00","id":1517847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517844#post1517844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps, but to be quite honest, I think a Garou's definition of making things &quot;better&quot; can be quite problematic, that said it got to the point of them replacing partriarch, I can think of a few lines of thinking of theirs that would get you into trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask Golgol Fangs First, Walks With Might, Margrave Yuri Konietzko, Elizabeth Genereader, Father Guiterrez and assorted others about what they did before the Apocalypse. Werewolves can do quite a bit of good when needed. The whole &quot;Garou fuck up forever and only thing they can ever do is make things worse&quot; is a meme. The whole point of the game is to BE BETTER, and there are many aspirational figures in the lore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517842#post1517842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's just that I recently re-read part of the silver fang book and there is a mention that humans wouldn't have a totem for them or a patronus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you might want to read some more about the Umbra and the spirits.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T20:25:49-07:00","id":1517856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517847#post1517847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ask Golgol Fangs First, Walks With Might, Margrave Yuri Konietzko, Elizabeth Genereader, Father Guiterrez and assorted others about what they did before the Apocalypse. Werewolves can do quite a bit of good when needed. The whole &quot;Garou fuck up forever and only thing they can ever do is make things worse&quot; is a meme. The whole point of the game is to BE BETTER, and there are many aspirational figures in the lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I am pretty much accustomed in be a vampire that dies like a dog to think different, but I will check out in the wikia anyway.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T20:26:32-07:00","id":1517857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517847#post1517847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you might want to read some more about the Umbra and the spirits.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe someday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T04:14:07-07:00","id":1517864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517847#post1517847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ask Golgol Fangs First, Walks With Might, Margrave Yuri Konietzko, Elizabeth Genereader, Father Guiterrez and assorted others about what they did before the Apocalypse. Werewolves can do quite a bit of good when needed. The whole &quot;Garou fuck up forever and only thing they can ever do is make things worse&quot; is a meme. The whole point of the game is to BE BETTER, and there are many aspirational figures in the lore.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>its probably worth noting that things are so objectively bad in wod that it's going to be a while before werewolf wins would become net negatives. For example even though they want to return mankind to the stone age, the more viable and relevant objective to wipe pentex out is a net positive.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T04:59:32-07:00","id":1517867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517864#post1517864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> its probably worth noting that things are so objectively bad in wod that it's going to be a while before werewolf wins would become net negatives. For example even though they want to return mankind to the stone age, the more viable and relevant objective to wipe pentex out is a net positive.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well. Returning mankind to the Stone Age isn't really an agreed upon course for the Garou. It's also not really viable, nor will it stop the Apocalypse at this point in time. Impergium was a solution for a while, but the moral, philosophical and human costs were too high. To shore up against the oncoming Apocalyptic tide that will hit the world the Garou have to:<ul><li>minimise infighting between themselves</li> <li>open communication and find ways to cooperate with the Fera</li> <li>find more allies among spirits willing to stick with them and honour the commitments to them</li> <li>fight off the avatars and monsters of the Wyrm that are direct threats to the planet</li> <li>sabotage and disable Wyrm operations that focus on making humanity its worst self</li> <li>support and communicate with humanity to reinforce them being their best self</li> </ul>Of course, fixing humanity may be a fool's errand, but it's the only real way to save the world long term. This is one of the reasons why I love Werewolf - the faults and errors of the Garou Nation are the faults and errors of Humanity, and the issues they need to resolve are mirrors to issues that plague us. In the end by depraving the Wyrm of human excess, pettiness and depravity they deprive the Wyrm of its power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T07:46:45-07:00","id":1517877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517867#post1517867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well. Returning mankind to the Stone Age isn't really an agreed upon course for the Garou. It's also not really viable, nor will it stop the Apocalypse at this point in time. Impergium was a solution for a while, but the moral, philosophical and human costs were too high. To shore up against the oncoming Apocalyptic tide that will hit the world the Garou have to:<ul><li>minimise infighting between themselves</li> <li>open communication and find ways to cooperate with the Fera</li> <li>find more allies among spirits willing to stick with them and honour the commitments to them</li> <li>fight off the avatars and monsters of the Wyrm that are direct threats to the planet</li> <li>sabotage and disable Wyrm operations that focus on making humanity its worst self</li> <li>support and communicate with humanity to reinforce them being their best self</li> </ul>Of course, fixing humanity may be a fool's errand, but it's the only real way to save the world long term. This is one of the reasons why I love Werewolf - the faults and errors of the Garou Nation are the faults and errors of Humanity, and the issues they need to resolve are mirrors to issues that plague us. In the end by depraving the Wyrm of human excess, pettiness and depravity they deprive the Wyrm of its power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much yeah....kinda. my point is by the time we get to the point where the garou nation could potentially be an existential threat. They would have collectively improved the lot of humanity as a byproduct of their agendas. Stuff like the annihilation of the vampires goes way before &quot;how many humans are okay and how high tech are they permitted for be.&quot;.<br /> <br /> in theory the garou could be antgonistic to humanity in the long run but at this moment our interests align.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T13:02:40-07:00","id":1517895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517818#post1517818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mra is more the mixture of the nameless angel, hellbringer and doge klypse. Father domain requires a degree of success lacking in MRA's. Personally I'd recommend working on the terfs and pushing for police reform.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the local ones seem pretty intent on doxing known feminists ( or really any woman with an online presence) and threatening to kill their pets/break into their homes, posting pics of their homes/places of employment and family members etc.<br /> <br /> Terfs and police reform are an ongoing concern but take a lot more time and resources than I personally have. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T13:38:37-07:00","id":1517900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517895#post1517895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, the local ones seem pretty intent on doxing known feminists ( or really any woman with an online presence) and threatening to kill their pets/break into their homes, posting pics of their homes/places of employment and family members etc.<br /> <br /> Terfs and police reform are an ongoing concern but take a lot more time and resources than I personally have. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds like Hellbringer in a low key petty loser way.<br /> <br /> Incels are more a failure to maintain dogma since you've failed to achieve exist inside rigid social expectations of Masculanity. Patriarch would despise them as men failing to be men as he would narrowly define it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-13-2023, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T18:53:28-07:00","id":1517997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517867#post1517867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]minimise infighting between themselves</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I think can be very difficult for some tribes, first of all the Red Talons and Wendigo, they don't talk to anyone outside, half the tribes wouldn't listen to the Glass Walkers and we have the dream foursome who take caerns. I don't even know where to start solving this problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517867#post1517867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]open communication and find ways to cooperate with the Fera</div> </div> </div> </div>In my view they trusted the Garou before and paid a very high price, it's true that these are different times, but even if one individual or another is trustworthy I recommend avoiding proximity, we can cooperate if the situation requires it, but keep it professional, or something like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517867#post1517867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b[*]find more allies among spirits willing to stick with them and honour the commitments to them</div> </div> </div> </div>Good Luck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517867#post1517867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]fight off the avatars and monsters of the Wyrm that are direct threats to the planet[*]sabotage and disable Wyrm operations that focus on making humanity its worst self</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't doing this already?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517867#post1517867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]support and communicate with humanity to reinforce them being their best self[/LIST]</div> </div> </div> </div>If I tell you that most people have no reason to even try.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517867#post1517867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, fixing humanity may be a fool's errand, but it's the only real way to save the world long term. This is one of the reasons why I love Werewolf - the faults and errors of the Garou Nation are the faults and errors of Humanity, and the issues they need to resolve are mirrors to issues that plague us. In the end by depraving the Wyrm of human excess, pettiness and depravity they deprive the Wyrm of its power.</div> </div> </div> </div>....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","user":"Psicose","date":". 07-14-2023, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T22:46:13-07:00","id":1518001,"title":"","content":"Even Incarna spirits can be destroyed, but the Maeljin Incarna seem to be a different class as they were once human who only ascended to Incarna status because of their Urge Wyrm patrons. And they get replaced if they do fall. Any Garou victory against one of the Maeljin is temporary at best because there will always be a number. The Patriarch spirit just seems to be a normal spirit, so I wouldn't apply the rules of the Maeljin to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T23:02:13-07:00","id":1518003,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517867#post1517867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well. Returning mankind to the Stone Age isn't really an agreed upon course for the Garou. It's also not really viable, nor will it stop the Apocalypse at this point in time. Impergium was a solution for a while, but the moral, philosophical and human costs were too high. To shore up against the oncoming Apocalyptic tide that will hit the world the Garou have to:<ul><li>minimise infighting between themselves</li> <li>open communication and find ways to cooperate with the Fera</li> <li>find more allies among spirits willing to stick with them and honour the commitments to them</li> <li>fight off the avatars and monsters of the Wyrm that are direct threats to the planet</li> <li>sabotage and disable Wyrm operations that focus on making humanity its worst self</li> <li>support and communicate with humanity to reinforce them being their best self</li> </ul>Of course, fixing humanity may be a fool's errand, but it's the only real way to save the world long term. This is one of the reasons why I love Werewolf - the faults and errors of the Garou Nation are the faults and errors of Humanity, and the issues they need to resolve are mirrors to issues that plague us. In the end by depraving the Wyrm of human excess, pettiness and depravity they deprive the Wyrm of its power.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point a &quot;hard reboot&quot; is what basically could save the World of Darkness<br /> Rorg, the Many-Taloned Hunter, is the Incarna of Turog, a destroyed planet that forms the Asteroid Belt did this in one of the Apocalypse scenarios - and if anyone, he could know, after all, Turog was destroyed by <i>a</i> Wyrm creature. Not <i>the</i> Wyrm. <i>A</i> Wyrm creature! So Rorg could be considered and expert when it comes to the Wyrm and its forces I belive<br /> Hurled a big asteroid to trigger an extcintion event.<br /> To be honest, not the worst of ideas... such an event would engulf the planet in cleansing fire, shatter the hold of the Wyrm, and more importantly, demolish the webs of the Weaver that choked the world.<br /> The Ordovician\u2013Silurian extinction event (or Late Ordovician mass extinction) happened 443 million years ago and eliminated 49\u201360% of marine genera and nearly 85% of marine species (In May 2020, studies suggested that the causes of the mass extinction were global warming, related to volcanism, and anoxia, but the deposition of volcanic ash has been suggested to be the trigger for reductions in atmospheric carbon dioxide leading to the glaciation and anoxia observed in the geological record have indicated global cooling as the primary driver)\u200b<br /> Th Late Devonian extinction extinction event happened 372 million years ago and overall, 19% of all families and 50% of all genera became extinct. (A recent study suggests that a nearby supernova explosion was the cause for the specific Hangenberg event, which marks the boundary between the Devonian and Carboniferous periods)<br /> The \u200bPermian\u2013Triassic extinction event happened 251.9 million years ago is the Earth's most severe known extinction event, with the extinction of 57% of biological families, 83% of genera, 81% of marine species and 70% of terrestrial vertebrate species. (Pinpointing the exact causes of the Permian\u2013Triassic extinction event is difficult, mostly because it occurred over 250 million years ago, and since then much of the evidence that would have pointed to the cause has been destroyed or is concealed deep within the Earth under many layers of rock. The sea floor is completely recycled over around 200 million years by the ongoing process of plate tectonics and seafloor spreading, leaving no useful indications beneath the ocean. But the best theory is the flood basalt eruptions that produced by the Siberian Traps increasing in atmospheric carbon dioxide with other emissions from the Siberian Traps)<br /> The Triassic\u2013Jurassic extinction event happened 201.4 million years ago and profoundly affected life on land and in the oceans. About 23% of all families, 48% of all genera (20% of marine families and 55% of marine genera) and 70% to 75% of all species became extinc (The leading and best evidenced explanation for the TJME is massive volcanic eruptions leading to ozone shield deterioration leading ti increased ultraviolet radiation flux)<br /> The Cretaceous\u2013Paleogene extinction event in approximately 66 million years ago caused the extinction of about 17% of all families, 50% of all genera and overall 75% of all species became extinct (caused by the impact of the giant Chicxulub asteroid or multiple impacts; other crater-like topographic features have also been proposed as impact craters formed in connection with Cretaceous\u2013Paleogene extinction. This suggests the possibility of near-simultaneous multiple impacts, perhaps from a fragmented asteroidal object. In addition to the 180 km Chicxulub crater, there is the 24 km Boltysh crater in Ukraine, the 20 km Silverpit crater in the North Sea, and the controversial and much larger 600 km Shiva crater. Any other craters that might have formed in the Tethys Ocean would since have been obscured by the northward tectonic drift of Africa and India.)<br /> So Earth/Gaiai is not unfamiliar with such event, large scale destructions, be it an asteroid or any other causes<br /> Nost surprisingly, one of the signs of the Apocalyps is the erruption of ALL the vulcanos on Earth...<br /> Bit fatalistic view but the best way to win the War for Gaia, kill the Patriarch and broke the Weaver's hold and tear the choking tendrils of the Wyrm off... would be another great extcinction event<br /> Amusingly enough, the Garou are even capable to do it...<br /> More amusing are the servitors of Zarok, the Incarna of Jupiter. The spirits of Callisto, Ganymede, Europa, Io, Adrastea, Amalthea, Thebe, Leda, Himalia, Lysithea, Elara, Ananke, Carine, Pasiphae, Sinoe and Metis <i>know</i> that Zarok is not merely another planet, but a small brown dwarf (a star that never achieved enough mass, then contracted enough to turn on its nuclear furnace). Rather viewing their liege as a star that failed, however, his court sees him as a star that might potentially become. Many of them are tired of Hyperion's position in the hierarchy of Incarnae and believe that if they could capture and use the Red Star's energy, they might light Zarok's fire. Then they themselves would become planets rather than merely moons. Since many of them are larger than some of the other planets, they do seem to have a point. Others among the court realize what sheer folly this would be, but their warnings have failed to interest the Incarna, who dismisses it as foolish jockeying for position. It's unclear whether Zarok actually agrees with and fosters his courtiers' designs or if he is simply too indulgent and unwilling to admit his mistake in housing his spirit minions in such a mighty physical forms so that they can keep him company and fawn on him. The conspirators will want to make use of any Garou visitors and try to involve them in the scheme. Finding out who's who, for if such a plan were to succeed, would mean Zarok would assume his place into being as a star. But it would also mean that Jupiter itself could burst into being a sun, this making the solar system a binary star system. Never mind that the exploding energy of the birth of a new star would destroy Earth and several other planets as well and would undoubtedly pulverize and disintegrate the very satellites who plot their lord's ascendence.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T02:33:52-07:00","id":1518016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1518001#post1518001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Incarna spirits can be destroyed, but the Maeljin Incarna seem to be a different class as they were once human who only ascended to Incarna status because of their Urge Wyrm patrons. And they get replaced if they do fall. Any Garou victory against one of the Maeljin is temporary at best because there will always be a number. The Patriarch spirit just seems to be a normal spirit, so I wouldn't apply the rules of the Maeljin to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhh, maybe? Even if you kill Patriarch the underlying concepts which allow it to exist will either force it to reform or create a new one.<br /> <br /> Also forcing Patriarch to manifest as the maeljin do could be an interesting plot arc on a number of levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T06:37:16-07:00","id":1518029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1518003#post1518003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point a &quot;hard reboot&quot; is what basically could save the World of Darkness<br /> Rorg, the Many-Taloned Hunter, is the Incarna of Turog, a destroyed planet that forms the Asteroid Belt did this in one of the Apocalypse scenarios - and if anyone, he could know, after all, Turog was destroyed by <i>a</i> Wyrm creature. Not <i>the</i> Wyrm. <i>A</i> Wyrm creature! So Rorg could be considered and expert when it comes to the Wyrm and its forces I belive<br /> Hurled a big asteroid to trigger an extcintion event.<br /> To be honest, not the worst of ideas... such an event would engulf the planet in cleansing fire, shatter the hold of the Wyrm, and more importantly, demolish the webs of the Weaver that choked the world.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> More amusing are the servitors of Zarok, the Incarna of Jupiter. The spirits of Callisto, Ganymede, Europa, Io, Adrastea, Amalthea, Thebe, Leda, Himalia, Lysithea, Elara, Ananke, Carine, Pasiphae, Sinoe and Metis <i>know</i> that Zarok is not merely another planet, but a small brown dwarf (a star that never achieved enough mass, then contracted enough to turn on its nuclear furnace). Rather viewing their liege as a star that failed, however, his court sees him as a star that might potentially become. Many of them are tired of Hyperion's position in the hierarchy of Incarnae and believe that if they could capture and use the Red Star's energy, they might light Zarok's fire. Then they themselves would become planets rather than merely moons. Since many of them are larger than some of the other planets, they do seem to have a point. Others among the court realize what sheer folly this would be, but their warnings have failed to interest the Incarna, who dismisses it as foolish jockeying for position. It's unclear whether Zarok actually agrees with and fosters his courtiers' designs or if he is simply too indulgent and unwilling to admit his mistake in housing his spirit minions in such a mighty physical forms so that they can keep him company and fawn on him. The conspirators will want to make use of any Garou visitors and try to involve them in the scheme. Finding out who's who, for if such a plan were to succeed, would mean Zarok would assume his place into being as a star. But it would also mean that Jupiter itself could burst into being a sun, this making the solar system a binary star system. Never mind that the exploding energy of the birth of a new star would destroy Earth and several other planets as well and would undoubtedly pulverize and disintegrate the very satellites who plot their lord's ascendence.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm well aware of all of this as well as numerous other scenarios the Shifters could do to cause a massive extinction level event if they really went about it. However, I do feel that the relative strength of the Wyrm is such that an event like that would wound Gaia beyond recovery while only eliminating a part of the physical threat on Earth. This would weaken Gaia allowing Anthelios and the final assault of the Wyrm to end her once and for all. Consider that the Wyrm was nowhere near as powerful during the last mass extinction. Now its forces in the Umbra are vast and ready to spring into action, and the defenders will have pretty much crippled themselves by doing this.<br /> <br /> I'm also quite wary of any solution that ends in genocide of Earth's biomass. That is a likely end scenario for many ways of how Apocalypse would go, but the Fera should be able to do something better than this, even if it costs all their lives to do it. After all it's their job and they may as well do something about it before everything goes to hell.<br /> <br /> Rorg is quite near and dear to me (and a key figure in two of my chronicles), but he's not quite all there. He was in his prime when he was torn apart and the scars that the event has left on him has made him quite specific in his interpretation of the world. Gaia is at her weakest, stuck in a slumber she may never wake from, she's bound not to weather his kind caress very well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T06:39:34-07:00","id":1518030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517997#post1517997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which I think can be very difficult for some tribes, first of all the Red Talons and Wendigo, they don't talk to anyone outside, half the tribes wouldn't listen to the Glass Walkers and we have the dream foursome who take caerns. I don't even know where to start solving this problem.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Good Luck.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> If I tell you that most people have no reason to even try.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>God forbid us doing anything that's hard. That would be horrible and never ever amount to anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1517997#post1517997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> ....<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, what pray tell, are your chronicles of Werewolf about?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T13:42:32-07:00","id":1518076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1517736-should-you-be-able-to-kill-the-patriarch?p=1518030#post1518030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> God forbid us doing anything that's hard. That would be horrible and never ever amount to anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, what pray tell, are your chronicles of Werewolf about?</div> </div> </div> </div>First: same thing here.<br /> Second: For me? A lost fight, that you still fighting no because you hope one day you will win, just because you really can't stay quiet and do nothing or just have a personal reason, something like avenge you family or lover, basically it's like fighting HIV, you can fight and maybe feel like it's worth the effort, but one day you'll lose, either for external reasons or simply because you don't have the fire left to keep going. Depressing, but not as bad as it sounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T14:27:59-07:00","id":1518087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/